# ⚠️ But the better way: make it available globally

So you don’t have to write DB queries in every Blade.

---

## ✅ Option A — Share it through a Service Provider (recommended)

### 1) Open `AppServiceProvider.php`

`app/Providers/AppServiceProvider.php`

### 2) Add this inside `boot()`:

```php
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\DB;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\View;

public function boot()
{
    $currency = DB::table('config')->first()->currency_symbol ?? 'KES';

    View::share('currencySymbol', $currency);
}
```

### 3) Now use it anywhere in Blade:

```php
<span class="reguler">{{ $currencySymbol }} {{ $product->price }}</span>
```

And elsewhere:

```php
{{ $currencySymbol }} {{ $order->total }}
{{ $currencySymbol }} {{ $cartTotal }}
{{ $currencySymbol }} {{ $shipping_fee }}
```

No more DB lookups in each page.

---

## ✅ Option B — Helper function (also good)

Create file:

`app/helpers.php`

```php
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\DB;

function currency_symbol()
{
    return DB::table('config')->first()->currency_symbol ?? 'KES';
}
```

Register helper in `composer.json` autoload:

```json
"files": [
    "app/helpers.php"
]
```

Then:

```bash
composer dump-autoload
```

Use anywhere:

```php
<span class="reguler">{{ currency_symbol() }} {{ $product->price }}</span>
```

